# Findings gitleaks may skip, by fingerprint (file:rule:line). There are none: the Supabase publishable keys
# (sb_publishable_… in config.js, config/demo.js and CONTRACT.md: made for browsers, served publicly, guarded by
# row-level security) are allowed by their value in .gitleaks.toml, and nothing else is. A fingerprint here would let
# any finding of that rule on that line through, a pasted secret key included, so add one only for a reviewed false
# positive that no value pattern can describe. Secret keys (sb_secret_…, service_role) must never be in this repository.
# Scan the commits of a branch before a push, not the working tree (whose ignored outputs, _site/ and config/local.js,
# are never committed):
#   gitleaks detect --source . --log-opts="origin/feat/platform-foundation..HEAD" --redact --no-banner
# tools/check-config.mjs checks that any entry here points at a publishable key.
